  "dom_id": "step-q41964",
  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "What is the range of the function $y=-4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x-{30}^{\u2218})+1?$",
  "worked_solution": "The range of $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x-{30}^{\u2218})\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-4$ and then adding $1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x-{30}^{\u2218})\\le 1 \\\\  & 4\\ge -4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x-{30}^{\u2218})\\ge -4 \\\\  & 5\\ge -4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x-{30}^{\u2218})+1\\ge -3 \\\\  & -3\\le y\\le 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in [-3,5].$",
